# Only the ordinary Linux gate uses this declaration. The client shards now
# run with delegated cgroup enforcement, so the shipped fixtures that once
# declined for want of helper enforcement execute for real and no longer
# need a waiver. What remains are skips outside that enforcement.
# The census also rejects this declaration if the skip stops occurring.

# The ordinary fast bucket does not install bwrap. The jailed Linux lane
# installs it and runs this exact tools test without a skip declaration.
declared|linux|SKIP git worktree: helper has no filesystem enforcement|The ordinary tools bucket cannot enforce the outside write; the jailed Linux lane runs the real Git worktree approval fixture with bubblewrap.

# The language-server manager's `gopls` fixture drives a real `gopls`
# through the jail on a two-package Go module. It is feature-detected: a
# runner without `gopls` (or without `go`, which `gopls` shells out to)
# prints this line and passes. The `gleam lsp` fixture beside it needs only
# the toolchain every runner has, so the manager's door, its jail and its
# probe are still exercised against a real server without this waiver.
declared|linux|SKIP lsp manager gopls: gopls or go is not installed|The ordinary runner installs no gopls; the gleam lsp fixture in the same file runs the whole door against a real jailed server, and a host with gopls on PATH or at ~/go/bin runs this one.

# The microVM executor fixture needs a hypervisor, the go-microvm runner, the
# Landlock guest kernel and an exported guest root (ADR-022); the hosted Linux
# runner carries none of them.
declared|linux|SKIP shipped microvm executor: LOOM_VM is unset|The microVM fixture needs a hypervisor and a built guest root; the hosted runner has neither, and it runs on a developer machine.

# The project template's copy-on-write fixture
# (`client/project_template_test`) runs only where `git-cow` is installed.
# Neither a hosted runner nor the signoff container carries it, and git-cow's
# Linux reflink path is unmeasured. The plain-copy fallback, which is what a
# host without git-cow uses, runs everywhere in the same module
# (`a_program_that_cannot_run_falls_back_to_the_plain_copy_test`). Remove this
# line once the runner installs a pinned git-cow.
declared|linux|SKIP project_template: git-cow is not installed|git-cow is not installed on hosted runners or in the signoff container; the plain-copy fallback runs in the same module.
